  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ccore#ElementAtRisk">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n16260563f62b42f1bc9a7e86ac636a9bb34"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n16260563f62b42f1bc9a7e86ac636a9bb35"/>
    <rdfs:comment>ElementAtRisk(O) --&gt;
∃ I, P. impactsOn(I, O), dpo:resultOf(I, P),
threatPerdurant(O, P) .</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>We say that an element is 'at risk' with respect to a certain threat perdurant if it is a service or a physical endurant for which an impact has been documented that results from the same threat perdurant and impacts on that element.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
