  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ccore#Goal">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment>"Things do not just have value, they have value for someone, and in case their aﬀordances enable certain happenings that positively contribute to the achievement of one's goals. Analogously, things are only at risk from one's perspective, in case their vulnerabilities enable happenings that hurt one's goals."
Sales, T. P., Baião, F., Guizzardi, G., Almeida, J. P. A., Guarino, N., &amp; Mylopoulos, J. (2018, September). The common ontology of value and risk. In International conference on conceptual modeling (pp. 121-135). Cham: Springer International Publishing.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
